# Turbulent Crater: "This land enters tapped unless your opponents control eight or more lands." On turn 19 Bot2 has seven
# lands and Bot1 has nine of its own, so Bot1's Crater enters tapped: its controller's lands are not the ones counted. On
# turn 20, with Bot1's ten lands out, Bot2's own Crater enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp x9
Turbulent Crater
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x7
Turbulent Crater
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Turbulent Crater.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Turbulent Crater.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 10
Bot2.Hand.Turbulent Crater.Play
? Bot2.Battlefield.Turbulent Crater.Tapped = false

[Expect]
Turn = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 10
Bot1.Battlefield.Turbulent Crater.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 8
Bot2.Battlefield.Turbulent Crater.Tapped = false
